      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "NYC Weekend Watch is our weekly round-up of repertory offerings."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "BAM A series on female possession begins while Ken Russell’s reconstructed The Devils continues—read (or listen to) our interview with Mark Kermode on it.",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "series on female possession",
          "url": "https://www.bam.org/film/2026/the-spirit"
        },
        {
          "text": "The Devils",
          "url": "https://www.bam.org/film/2026/the-devils"
        },
        {
          "text": "interview with Mark Kermode",
          "url": "https://thefilmstage.com/i-cant-quite-believe-its-happening-mark-kermode-on-resurrecting-ken-russells-the-devils/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Roxy Cinema A print of The Texas Chain Saw Massacre plays on Friday and Saturday, the latter day bringing Silent Night, Deadly Night 5 on 35mm and Suspiria ; Halloween shows on Friday and Saturday while Ganja & Hess screens on Sunday.",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "The Texas Chain Saw Massacre",
          "url": "https://www.roxycinemanewyork.com/screenings/the-texas-chainsaw-massacre-35mm/"
        },
        {
          "text": "Silent Night, Deadly Night 5",
          "url": "https://www.roxycinemanewyork.com/screenings/silent-night-deadly-night-5-the-toy-maker-35mm-the-surreal-nightmares-of-screaming-mad-george/"
        },
        {
          "text": "Suspiria",
          "url": "https://www.roxycinemanewyork.com/screenings/suspiria/"
        },
        {
          "text": "Halloween",
          "url": "https://www.roxycinemanewyork.com/screenings/halloween/"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ganja & Hess",
          "url": "https://www.roxycinemanewyork.com/screenings/ganja-hess/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Museum of Modern Art A Sergei Loznitsa retrospective continues while Sundays with Steven starts with 2005’s War of the Worlds and 1953’s on 35mm.",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Sergei Loznitsa retrospective",
          "url": "https://www.moma.org/calendar/film/5937"
        },
        {
          "text": "War of the Worlds",
          "url": "https://www.moma.org/calendar/events/11779"
        },
        {
          "text": "1953’s",
          "url": "https://www.moma.org/calendar/events/11778"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Film Forum A 4K restoration of Alexander Payne’s Citizen Ruth begins playing; Coco shows on Sunday.",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Citizen Ruth",
          "url": "https://filmforum.org/film/citizen-ruth"
        },
        {
          "text": "Coco",
          "url": "https://filmforum.org/film/coco-ffjr-2026"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Anthology Film Archives A Troma series continues while films by Frampton, Franju, Jean Genet, and Ernie Gehr show in Essential Cinema .",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Troma series",
          "url": "https://www.anthologyfilmarchives.org/film_screenings/series/62026"
        },
        {
          "text": "Essential Cinema",
          "url": "https://www.anthologyfilmarchives.org/film_screenings/programs/essential-cinema"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Museum of the Moving Image The international version of The Shining makes its U.S. premiere on Sunday, followed by the theatrical cut ; Goodbye, Dragon Inn shows on Friday; The Exorcist and a print of Poltergeist are featured in Handcrafted Horror .",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "The Shining",
          "url": "https://movingimage.org/event/the-shining-international-version/"
        },
        {
          "text": "the theatrical cut",
